WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.105
Magrib was certain that Aladdin was the right boy.

2
00:00:19.106 --> 00:00:25.346
He reached his long arm into the crowd of children and grabbed Aladdin's sleeve.

3
00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:31.659
"Come here, my boy," he said.

4
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:36.531
"Tell me—are you the son of a poor tailor?"

5
00:00:36.532 --> 00:00:42.290
"Oh yes, I am," said Aladdin, "but my father died years ago."

6
00:00:42.291 --> 00:00:45.535
"He's dead?" cried the magician.

7
00:00:45.536 --> 00:00:55.623
With a groan, he threw his arms around Aladdin's neck and began to weep.

8
00:00:55.624 --> 00:00:57.057
"Why are you crying?"

9
00:00:57.058 --> 00:01:00.810
asked Aladdin, his eyes wide with surprise.

10
00:01:00.811 --> 00:01:04.031
"Did you know my father?"

11
00:01:04.032 --> 00:01:08.166
"Did I know him?" exclaimed the magician.

12
00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.461
"Your father was my brother!

13
00:01:11.462 --> 00:01:14.643
And now you say he is dead!"

14
00:01:14.644 --> 00:01:17.805
Tears poured down his cheeks.

15
00:01:17.806 --> 00:01:20.851
"I am Magrib, your uncle.

16
00:01:20.852 --> 00:01:25.150
I have traveled over deserts and mountains to see him.

17
00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:30.900
But I am too late!"

18
00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.235
"I'm so sorry," said Aladdin.

19
00:01:33.236 --> 00:01:35.754
"My father never spoke of you."

20
00:01:35.755 --> 00:01:40.095
"The moment I saw you, I knew you were my brother's son,"

21
00:01:40.096 --> 00:01:43.689
murmured Magrib, still weeping.

22
00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:45.579
"You look just like him.

23
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.194
Your handsome nose!

24
00:01:47.195 --> 00:01:49.935
Your black eyes!"

25
00:01:49.936 --> 00:01:53.734
He squeezed Aladdin closer to his chest.

26
00:01:53.735 --> 00:02:02.774
"Oh, my child, I must accept God's will and take comfort that you, my own nephew, are alive and well.

27
00:02:02.775 --> 00:02:05.526
Now tell me, where do you live?

28
00:02:05.527 --> 00:02:09.486
Where is your mother, my brother's wife?"

29
00:02:09.487 --> 00:02:15.816
Aladdin led Magrib to a street of crooked houses made of mud and wood.

30
00:02:15.817 --> 00:02:19.581
"Just go to the end of the road and you will be at our door."

31
00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:27.343
Instead, Magrib reached into his sleeve and brought out five gold coins.

32
00:02:27.344 --> 00:02:28.958
"Go," he said.

33
00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:33.459
"Take these to your mother and tell her that your uncle has come.

34
00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.565
This evening I will visit my brother's house.

35
00:02:36.566 --> 00:02:40.797
Tell your mother to prepare a fine meal for us all."

36
00:02:40.798 --> 00:02:43.228
"I will happily do as you say, my uncle!"

37
00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:47.193
said Aladdin, amazed at the coins in his hands.

38
00:02:47.194 --> 00:02:53.419
He had never seen so much money, and he ran home as fast as he could.

39
00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.872
When Aladdin arrived, his mother was busy spinning yarn.

40
00:02:57.873 --> 00:03:00.882
She was surprised to see her son.

41
00:03:00.883 --> 00:03:07.042
"I never see you except at mealtime," she said, "and supper is hours away.

42
00:03:07.043 --> 00:03:09.951
What do you want from me?"

43
00:03:09.952 --> 00:03:13.393
"Mother!" he cried. "I have great news!

44
00:03:13.394 --> 00:03:15.995
I bring greetings from my uncle!"

45
00:03:15.996 --> 00:03:20.778
"Uncle?" said Zeba. "You have no uncle!"

46
00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:24.470
"Listen," replied Aladdin. "It is true!"

47
00:03:24.471 --> 00:03:30.118
The boy told her everything that had happened and all that Magrib had said.

48
00:03:30.119 --> 00:03:33.618
Then Aladdin gave his mother the coins.

49
00:03:33.619 --> 00:03:36.135
They sparkled in her hand.

50
00:03:36.136 --> 00:03:39.468
"Your father never spoke of a brother," she said.

51
00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:41.751
"Is it possible?"

52
00:03:41.752 --> 00:03:44.489
"Yes, Mother," said Aladdin.

53
00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.835
"And my uncle is coming to eat with us tonight!"

54
00:03:46.836 --> 00:03:49.589
"Tonight!" cried Zeba.

55
00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.903
"I must get ready!

56
00:03:50.904 --> 00:03:53.765
There is so much to do!"

57
00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:57.777
Aladdin's mother took the coins and hurried to the market.

58
00:03:57.778 --> 00:04:02.216
She bought olive oil, cheese, and a plump chicken.

59
00:04:02.217 --> 00:04:08.377
Back at home, she set out her best dishes and laid out a colorful dinner cloth.

60
00:04:08.378 --> 00:04:12.085
She baked bread and toasted almonds.

61
00:04:12.086 --> 00:04:17.659
Finally the meal was ready, but Magrib had not yet arrived.

62
00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.670
"Well, where is he?" asked Zeba.

63
00:04:20.671 --> 00:04:23.957
"Maybe he got lost," said Aladdin.

64
00:04:23.958 --> 00:04:27.605
"Lost?" said his mother. "You may be right.

65
00:04:27.606 --> 00:04:30.144
Run to the corner and look for him!"

66
00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:36.535
Just then they heard a knock on their door.
